\par }{\b\insrsid10890595  Solid waste refers to solid materials that result from human activities which generates useless, unwanted or obsolete mater
ials. Most often than not, these materials are hazardous especially in the case of toxic waste. Therefore it raises the need for the proper disposal of such materials to prevent an adverse effect on the environment. The quantity in which they are produced
 is another factor of concern. Some negative effects on the environment include:
\par }\pard \ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\sl360\slmult1\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\faauto\rin0\lin720\itap0\pararsid2701497 {\b\insrsid10890595 1.}{\b\insrsid3212325  }{\b\insrsid10890595 
Air pollution resulting from bad odour evolving from decomposition of putrescible goods or organic waste.
\par 2.}{\b\insrsid3212325  }{\b\insrsid10890595 Water pollution which arises from leach ate during heavy rainfall. Both surface and ground water are affected in this wise. 
\par 3. Depletion of the ozone layer resulting from the release of toxins into the atmosphere causing green house effect.  
\par 4.}{\b\insrsid3212325  }{\b\insrsid10890595 Outbreak of diseases resulting from the favourable conditions created that serves as breading grounds for germs and bacteria. 
\par 5.}{\b\insrsid3212325  }{\b\insrsid10890595 Creating of unsightly scenes. 
\par }\pard \ql \li360\ri0\sl360\slmult1\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\faauto\rin0\lin360\itap0\pararsid2701497 {\insrsid556051 
